  "mechanisms": [
    "Reuse the counter-relative CFG worklist, shared affine entry identities and decoded register/memory footprints for source-backed directory cursors; nested DBF uses the same conservative joins rather than enumerating path/iteration combinations.",
    "Keep type domains separate from exact pointer packets. A native loop envelope validates every covered pointer entry against canonical source ownership and a compatible declared record view. It carries zero numeric candidates, no inline pointer expression, and no changed four-candidate cap.",
    "Reuse one canonical source-record view resolver for compact packed arrays and expanded record fields; conflicting, null, interior, code-overlapping and incompatible targets do not acquire the directory type.",
    "CPU writes must be disjoint from the directory envelope and every instruction used by the proof. Known carried source/raw address roots and decoded spans include 24-bit bus aliases; unknown writes/calls and wrapping envelopes refuse. Losing an unrelated old source register no longer discards an otherwise valid directory cursor; a write through a lost pointer still refuses.",
    "The shared decoded register-write mask now includes the conditional low-WORD DBcc counter write. A DBF/DBNE cannot retain an unchanged LONG address identity. The prior stale-identity assertion fails on the old implementation and passes on this one.",
    "A stationary zero-stride loop keeps direct app symbols only when the original base displacement is zero and the original operand/access width matches. Moving/interior loops still cannot borrow a direct-base symbol; fallback provenance is not promoted to a proved base."
  ],
